WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:05.600
Welcome to the weirdest city in Alaska, Whittier.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.510
But Whittier is the city that forgot how to
city, because it is home to just 220 people,

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:14.950
and they all live in one building.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:19.040
Yep, everyone lives in this monolithic tower
block of condos.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.690
Except this one guy who thinks he’s a badass
and lives in a mobile home, right next door.

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:24.870
His name is Paul by the way.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:29.950
But Paul aside, this entire city’s residents
don’t just live in one building – they

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:33.660
go to work, school and do their shopping there
too.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:39.000
The 14-story building is called Begich Tower
and houses not only residential condos for

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.420
220 people, but everything else you need to
live.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:48.280
The building contains a police station, two
grocery stores, the city offices, an indoor

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:53.450
playground, a B&amp;B, a Laundromat, a post office,
a health clinic and a school.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:58.370
Okay it doesn’t have a Hooters, so not quite
everything you need to live, but close enough.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:02.489
Oh did I forget to mention, there’s also
a church in the basement.

00:01:02.489 --> 00:01:04.949
God knows why it’s in the basement.

00:01:04.949 --> 00:01:10.030
Residents of Whittier enjoy pure isolation
and live mostly off the land, catching fish

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.000
and other local wildlife.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.950
Not only is Whittier encased on all sides
by towering mountains and a lake but there

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:23.530
is only one road to and from the city which
completely closes at night.

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:28.299
The road is a single lane tunnel through a
mountain that only goes one way at a time;

00:01:28.299 --> 00:01:32.549
the direction of the road changes at specific
times throughout the day.

00:01:32.549 --> 00:01:35.950
On the plus side, crime rates are low, since
thieves have to wait for the road to change

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:41.439
direction before making their grand getaway,
which is awfully inconvenient.

00:01:41.439 --> 00:01:47.189
Whittier poses a strange dichotomy – with
its extreme isolation and low population you

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:51.850
would think it’s a place for loners and
introverts, the kind of place where your weird

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:55.549
cousin Kevin might emigrate too and you never
see him again.

00:01:55.549 --> 00:01:59.780
But on the other hand you couldn’t move
to a more interactive, social environment

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:05.650
than Whittier; you are literally living underneath,
on top of and next to the entire city’s

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:06.650
population.

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:10.750
You better hope you get on with your neighbours,
because they never bloody change.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:15.660
Residents regularly shuffle around the building’s
many public hallways and rooms in their pajamas

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:21.040
and underwear, bestowed with an unusual level
of comfort and familiarity with their neighbours.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:25.099
If school students get stuck with their homework
they simply knock on the teacher’s door

00:02:25.099 --> 00:02:27.670
for help, after all, she only lives down the
hall.

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:31.790
But there’s a damn good reason these residents
have everything they need in one building

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:36.860
and rarely set foot outdoors, at least in
the winter… because the entire place is

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.430
trying to kill you.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:44.120
During the harsh winter months Whittier is
encased in a metre of snow, and being on the

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:51.099
waterfront in are-you-sure-you-want-to-go-outside
Alaska, it’s constantly blasted by 60 mph

00:02:51.099 --> 00:02:57.430
winds and because it’s seriously-though-there’s-bears-out-there
Alasaka there are lots of bears about.

00:02:57.430 --> 00:03:01.630
This is the reason the children’s playground
is indoors and school kids have to pass through

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:07.040
an underground tunnel to go to school, which
is in a building adjacent to Begich Tower,

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.840
connected only by this passageway.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:14.680
Just try telling the people of Whittier that
winter is coming, trust me, they know.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:19.120
There’s even an indoor vegetable garden
maintained by the school kids to provide sustenance

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:20.120
through the winter.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:24.200
The vegetables are grown using hydroponic
equipment donated by the police after they

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.090
seized it during a drugs raid.

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:28.000
Here you go kids grow some herbs.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.870
It only takes a smart kid with access to the
internet to realize they have everything they

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:33.800
need to start a pot farm.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:39.890
So you’ve got to ask the question, why do
these people do it, apart from amazing views

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:42.849
and the occasional rooftop barbeque?

00:03:42.849 --> 00:03:47.140
Well most of these people didn’t move here
out of choice, they simply found themselves

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.269
living in Whittier, out of circumstance.

00:03:49.269 --> 00:03:54.610
You see Whittier was built during World War
II as a military facility for the United States

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:55.610
Army.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:04:00.150
They wanted a base somewhere secluded and
protected by the mountains, well congratulations,

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.420
you found it.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:04.500
Begich Tower was built as barracks to house
the military.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:10.260
The location was owned by the government until
1969, when it was given to the residents and

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:11.411
officially became a city.

00:04:11.411 --> 00:04:17.709
The people who live there now are simply the
remnants of the military base that once was,

00:04:17.709 --> 00:04:21.060
the descendants of soldiers and workers who
resided there.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:26.389
There isn’t much demand for property in
Whittier from outsiders and the population

00:04:26.389 --> 00:04:28.740
is slowly decreasing every year.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:33.259
It does draw a huge tourist trade during the
summer months though, because of it’s peculiarity

00:04:33.259 --> 00:04:34.699
and natural beauty.

00:04:34.699 --> 00:04:40.919
If you intend to visit Whittier, you better
do so fast before Begich Tower bids its final

00:04:40.919 --> 00:04:47.020
farewell, much to the dismay of its loyal
220 residents.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:05:20.719
Except Paul, he doesn’t care, he’s got
his mobile home.

